-- ============================================================================
-- T2 - Digital Services Act: very large online platforms
-- Instrument : Regulation (EU) 2022/2065 (Digital Services Act)
--              http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj
-- Pinpoint   : Art 33(1), (4), (6)
-- Version    : OJ L 277, 27.10.2022, p. 1 (original text) - NOT CHECKED. EUR-Lex was
--              blocked from the spike environment, so the text below is quoted from
--              the author's knowledge and must be verified before reliance.
-- Evaluated  : 2026-09-23
-- Operative text (UNVERIFIED):
--   Art 33(1): This Section shall apply to online platforms and online search
--     engines which have a number of average monthly active recipients of the
--     service in the Union equal to or higher than 45 million, and which are
--     designated as very large online platforms or very large online search
--     engines pursuant to paragraph 4.
--   Art 33(4): The Commission shall ... adopt a decision designating as a very
--     large online platform ... the online platform ... which has a number of
--     average monthly active recipients of the service equal to or higher than the
--     number referred to in paragraph 1 ...
--   Art 33(6): The obligations set out in this Section shall apply, or cease to
--     apply, to the very large online platforms and very large online search
--     engines concerned from four months after the notification to the provider
--     concerned referred to in paragraph 5.
-- Modelling: the four-month period runs from NOTIFICATION (Art 33(5)-(6)), not from
-- the designation decision, so the notification date is the input.
-- ============================================================================

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT kleene

§ `DSA Art 33 - very large online platforms`
@ref-map dsa-art33 https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2022/2065/oj#art_33

DECLARE `VLOP status` IS ONE OF
    `Threshold not met`
    `Threshold met, not designated`
    `Designated, obligations not yet applicable`
    `Designated, obligations applicable`

@ref dsa-art33 Art 33(1)
GIVEN `average monthly active EU recipients` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`VLOP threshold met` MEANS
    `at least` `average monthly active EU recipients` 45000000

@ref dsa-art33 Art 33(6)
GIVEN `evaluation date`   IS A DATE
      `notification date` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`obligations not yet applicable` MEANS
    `before` `evaluation date` (`months after maybe` 4 `notification date`)

@export VLOP status under DSA Art 33 on the evaluation date. Returns every status still possible; one item means settled.
@ref dsa-art33 Art 33(1), (4), (6)
GIVEN `evaluation date`                      IS A DATE           @desc date the question is asked (ISO 8601)
      `average monthly active EU recipients` IS A MAYBE NUMBER   @desc Art 33(1) figure; null if unknown
      `designated as VLOP`                   IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Commission designation under Art 33(4); null if unknown
      `notification date`                    IS A MAYBE DATE     @desc date the designation was notified to the provider (Art 33(5)); null if unknown
GIVETH A LIST OF `VLOP status`
`VLOP status on` MEANS
    `possible outcomes`
        (LIST (PAIR OF (`not` (`VLOP threshold met` `average monthly active EU recipients`)), `Threshold not met`),
              (PAIR OF (`not` `designated as VLOP`), `Threshold met, not designated`),
              (PAIR OF (`obligations not yet applicable` `evaluation date` `notification date`), `Designated, obligations not yet applicable`))
        `Designated, obligations applicable`
